Found while implementing the objectui half of objectstack-ai/objectstack#8018. Filed rather than fixed there: the file is held by an in-flight sibling (objectstack-ai/objectstack#8499 declares `packages/app-shell/src/views/RecordDetailView.tsx`), so touching it would have been a scope breach.

## The shape

`packages/app-shell/src/views/RecordDetailView.tsx:617-621`:

```ts
if (action.recordIdParam) {
  const rowField = (action as any).recordIdField || 'id';
  const rowValue = ...;
  if (rowValue != null) body[action.recordIdParam] = rowValue;
}
```

The empty `else` is the defect, and it is the same one objectstack-ai/objectstack#8018 measured on the console action runtime: when the record cannot supply the key, the parameter is dropped and **the request goes out anyway**. A backend that reads a missing selector as "match nothing" answers success for having changed nothing, so a record-scoped mutation reports success and does nothing.

## Why it is not already covered

The projection half of the #8018 fix does not reach this surface — a detail view fetches the whole record rather than a listView projection, so the *ordinary* absent-key route is closed here. The remaining routes are real though:

- a server-side read mask that strips the field regardless of what was asked for (`internal: true` on the field);
- a field the current principal cannot read;
- a genuine `null` value on the record.

In all three the current code sends an under-specified request instead of refusing.

## The repair

One line. The guard already exists as a shared helper, put in `@object-ui/core` for exactly this reason:

```ts
import { resolveRecordIdParamSeed } from '@object-ui/core';

const seed = resolveRecordIdParamSeed(action, rowRecord);
if (seed.error) return { success: false, error: seed.error };
if (seed.value !== undefined) body[action.recordIdParam!] = seed.value;
```

`resolveRecordIdParamSeed` distinguishes an absent key from a null value and words the two refusals differently, because they point at different repairs. Unit coverage is in `packages/core/src/actions/__tests__/recordIdParam.test.ts`.

## Note for whoever picks this up

`scripts/check-action-forward-parity.mjs` derives its owed set from property accesses on the `action` binding. `RecordDetailView.tsx` currently reads `(action as any).recordIdField`, which that extractor does not see (the cast breaks the identifier match). Routing this site through the helper is neutral for the gate — the helper is already registered as a runtime consumer — but the `as any` cast there is worth dropping while you are in the file, so the gate can see the surface honestly.

Backlink: objectstack-ai/objectstack#8018 (the general half, landed in objectui); PR objectstack-ai/objectui#PENDING.

